        "problem": "The parabola ${x}^{2}=4(y+5)$ intersects the $y$-axis at the point$\\,(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$",
        "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4(y+5) \\\\ (0)^{2} & =4(y+5) \\\\ 0 & =4y+20 \\\\ 4y & =-20 \\\\ y & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $y$-axis at $(0,-5).$",
